    <item>
      <title>Cascade filtering in SAC</title>
      <link>http://localhost:54161/posts/sac-app-dropdown-cascade/</link>
      <pubDate>Sun, 12 Dec 2021 15:42:26 +0100</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:54161/posts/sac-app-dropdown-cascade/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;In this part of the tutorial, we are focusing on creating a cascade filter on the dropdown in SAC APP.
Cascade means that filters on the dashboard will depend on each other. In the example, if you pick up the publisher name Nintendo then in the games list (Name) you should see only games that belong to Nintendo and no more others. To achieve this, we have to redesign our app a bit.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Create and fill a dropdown in SAC APP</title>
      <link>http://localhost:54161/posts/sac-app-dropdown/</link>
      <pubDate>Sun, 12 Dec 2021 14:13:53 +0100</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:54161/posts/sac-app-dropdown/</guid>
      <description>&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Firstly we have to move our table a few lines down. This can be done by moving the mouse between the table and toolbar and drag and dropping when the cursor changes the icon:
&lt;figure class=&#34;align-center &#34;&gt;
    &lt;img loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;http://localhost:54161/sac_app_dropdown/1.png#center&#34; width=&#34;80%&#34;/&gt; 
&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Click on the plus icon on the toolbar
&lt;figure class=&#34;align-center &#34;&gt;
    &lt;img loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;http://localhost:54161/sac_app_dropdown/2.png#center&#34; width=&#34;80%&#34;/&gt; 
&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Select Dropdown form the list
&lt;figure class=&#34;align-center &#34;&gt;
    &lt;img loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;http://localhost:54161/sac_app_dropdown/3.png#center&#34; width=&#34;80%&#34;/&gt; 
&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lets rename the Table by click on tree dots -&amp;gt; Rename, and set new name to Table_Games_Sales
&lt;figure class=&#34;align-center &#34;&gt;
    &lt;img loading=&#34;lazy&#34; src=&#34;http://localhost:54161/sac_app_dropdown/5.png#center&#34; width=&#34;80%&#34;/&gt; 
&lt;/figure&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Same with Dropdown, and put new name Dropdown_Name&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
